/-!
# Coherence over a coherent structure sheaf

Let `(X, 𝒪)` be a ringed space whose structure sheaf is coherent as a module over itself, that
is, `SheafOfModules.unit 𝒪` is coherent in the sense of Tag 01BV. Stacks Tag 01BZ says that for
such a ringed space the coherent sheaves of modules are exactly the sheaves of modules of finite
presentation.

One implication is Tag 01BW and holds with no hypothesis on `𝒪`. The other is the content of
this file. A module of finite presentation is of finite type, so what has to be shown is the
second coherence condition: for every open `U`, every finite `I` and every map
`φ : 𝒪_U^I ⟶ F|_U`, the kernel of `φ` is of finite type. The argument reduces this to the case
of a map between finite free modules, where the coherence of `𝒪` applies, in four steps, each
step peeling off one layer:

* the target is a *finite free* module (`kernel_free_map_isFiniteType`): this is exactly
  coherence of `𝒪^J`, which holds because coherent modules are closed under finite coproducts;
* the target is finite free and the source is merely of *finite type*
  (`kernel_to_finite_free_isFiniteType`): cover by opens over which the source is generated by
  finitely many sections, use the previous step on the slice, and push the kernel back with
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_kernel_of_epi_comp`;
* the source is finite free and the target has a *global finite presentation*
  (`kernel_free_to_globalPresentation_isFiniteType`): add the generators of the presentation to
  the source, so that the combined map is an epimorphism from a finite free module onto a
  finitely presented module, whose kernel is of finite type by Tag 01BP; the kernel sought is
  then the kernel of a map from that one into a finite free module, which is the previous step;
* the target is of finite presentation (`kernel_free_to_finitePresentation_isFiniteType`): the
  previous step applies on each open of a cover witnessing the finite presentation, and being of
  finite type is local.

The third and fourth steps are needed on the *iterated* slice site, because the covers produced
by the second and fourth live over an open which is itself already a slice; `overOverEquivalence`
transports them.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isCoherent_iff_isFinitePresentation`: **Tag 01BZ.** Over a ringed space
  whose structure sheaf is coherent, a sheaf of modules is coherent if and only if it is of
  finite presentation.

## Implementation notes

The forward implication is `isFinitePresentation_of_isCoherent`, which states Tag 01BW for a
root-level `SheafOfModules.IsCoherent`, the same two-field class as
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent` but a different constant; the two are converted into each
other field by field where they meet. The duplication is not introduced here and is not resolved
here either.

Restriction to an open preserves being of finite presentation. That is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentation_over` of
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalOnCover.FinitePresentationSlice`, stated
there for an arbitrary site and used here at the site of opens, together with the
`exists_finitePresentation_overOver` it rests on.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BP)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace SheafOfModules

universe u v₁ u₁

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable {X : Type u} [TopologicalSpace X]

/-! ### Finite free modules over a coherent structure sheaf -/

section Free

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{u} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}

/-- The free module on `I` over the slice site at `U` is the restriction to `U` of the free
module on `I`. -/
private noncomputable def freeOverIso (R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}) (U : C) (I : Type u)
    [HasBinaryProducts C] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [∀ Y : C, HasSheafify (J.over Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [∀ Y : C, (J.over Y).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}] :
    free (R := R.over U) I ≅ (free (R := R) I).over U :=
  mapFreeIso (overFunctor R U) I (FiniteTypeKernel.unitOverIso U)

end Free

section RingedSpace

variable {R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}}

/-- Over a ringed space whose structure sheaf is coherent, every finite free module is
coherent: coherent modules are closed under finite coproducts. -/
private theorem isCoherent_free [IsCoherent (unit R)] (I : Type u) [Finite I] :
    IsCoherent (free (R := R) I) :=
  (coherentModules R).prop_of_iso
    (IsColimit.coconePointUniqueUpToIso (coproductIsCoproduct (fun _ : I => unit R))
      (isColimitFreeCofan I))
    (isCoherent_sigma (fun _ : I => unit R) fun _ => inferInstance)

/-- The kernel of a map between finite free modules on a slice site is of finite type. This is
coherence of the finite free target, read on the slice at `U`. -/
private theorem kernel_free_map_isFiniteType (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u})
    [IsCoherent (unit R)] (U : Opens X) (I K : Type u) [Finite I] [Finite K]
    (f : free (R := R.over U) I ⟶ free (R := R.over U) K) : (kernel f).IsFiniteType := by
  have : IsCoherent (free (R := R) K) := isCoherent_free K
  have hK : (kernel (f ≫ (freeOverIso R U K).hom)).IsFiniteType :=
    IsCoherent.kernel_isFiniteType U I inferInstance (f ≫ (freeOverIso R U K).hom)
  exact isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (kernelCompMono f (freeOverIso R U K).hom)

/-- The same on the iterated slice site: the kernel of a map between finite free modules on the
slice at `V` over the slice at `U` is of finite type. -/
private theorem kernel_free_map_isFiniteType_over
    (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}) [IsCoherent (unit R)]
    (U : Opens X) (V : Over U) (I K : Type u) [Finite I] [Finite K]
    (f : free (R := (R.over U).over V) I ⟶ free (R := (R.over U).over V) K) :
    (kernel f).IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  set E := overOverEquivalence (R := R) U V with hE
  have hpc : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} E.inverse := inferInstance
  set a := mapFreeIso E.inverse I (Iso.refl _) with ha
  set b := mapFreeIso E.inverse K (Iso.refl _) with hb
  have hg : (kernel (a.hom ≫ E.inverse.map f ≫ b.inv)).IsFiniteType :=
    kernel_free_map_isFiniteType R V.left I K _
  have h₁ : (kernel (E.inverse.map f)).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_of_iso.{u}
      (kernel.mapIso (a.hom ≫ E.inverse.map f ≫ b.inv) (E.inverse.map f) a b (by simp))
  have h₂ : (E.inverse.obj (kernel f)).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (PreservesKernel.iso E.inverse f).symm
  exact isFiniteType_of_overOverEquivalence_inverse U V h₂

/-- The kernel of a map from a module of finite type into a finite free module, on a slice site,
is of finite type. -/
private theorem kernel_to_finite_free_isFiniteType
    (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}) [IsCoherent (unit R)]
    (U : Opens X) (K : Type u) [Finite K] {F : SheafOfModules.{u} (R.over U)} [F.IsFiniteType]
    (f : F ⟶ free (R := R.over U) K) : (kernel f).IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData F
  have hLocal : ∀ i, ((kernel f).over (q.X i)).IsFiniteType := by
    intro i
    have hfin : Finite (q.generators i).I := (hq.isFiniteType i).finite
    -- On the slice at `q.X i` the source becomes a quotient of a finite free module.
    have hcomp : (kernel ((q.generators i).π ≫ f.over (q.X i))).IsFiniteType := by
      have := kernel_free_map_isFiniteType_over R U (q.X i) (q.generators i).I K
        ((q.generators i).π ≫ f.over (q.X i) ≫ (freeOverIso (R.over U) (q.X i) K).inv)
      exact isFiniteType_of_iso.{u}
        (kernelCompMono ((q.generators i).π ≫ f.over (q.X i))
          (freeOverIso (R.over U) (q.X i) K).inv)
    have hpsi : (kernel (f.over (q.X i))).IsFiniteType :=
      isFiniteType_kernel_of_epi_comp (q.generators i).π (f.over (q.X i)) hcomp
    have : PreservesFiniteLimits (overFunctor.{u} (R.over U) (q.X i)) :=
      LocalCokernel.overFunctor_preservesFiniteLimits (q.X i)
    exact isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (overKernelIso f (q.X i)).symm
  exact isFiniteType_of_coversTop (kernel f) q.X q.coversTop

/-- The kernel of `f` is the kernel of the second projection restricted to the kernel of
`biprod.desc f p`. -/
private noncomputable def kernelOfBiprodDescIso {A : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} A] [Abelian A]
    {Y Z W : A} (f : Y ⟶ W) (p : Z ⟶ W) :
    kernel f ≅ kernel (kernel.ι (biprod.desc f p) ≫ (biprod.snd : Y ⊞ Z ⟶ Z)) := by
  let g : Y ⊞ Z ⟶ W := biprod.desc f p
  let h : kernel g ⟶ Z := kernel.ι g ≫ biprod.snd
  let a : kernel f ⟶ kernel g :=
    kernel.lift g (kernel.ι f ≫ biprod.inl) (by simp [g, Category.assoc])
  have ha : a ≫ h = 0 := by simp [a, h, Category.assoc]
  have hk : kernel.ι h ≫ kernel.ι g =
      (kernel.ι h ≫ kernel.ι g ≫ biprod.fst) ≫ (biprod.inl : Y ⟶ Y ⊞ Z) := by
    refine biprod.hom_ext _ _ ?_ ?_
    · simp [Category.assoc]
    · simp [h, Category.assoc]
  have hb : (kernel.ι h ≫ kernel.ι g ≫ biprod.fst) ≫ f = 0 := by
    calc
      _ = ((kernel.ι h ≫ kernel.ι g ≫ biprod.fst) ≫ biprod.inl) ≫ g := by
        simp [g, Category.assoc]
      _ = kernel.ι h ≫ kernel.ι g ≫ g := by
        simpa only [Category.assoc] using congrArg (fun t => t ≫ g) hk.symm
      _ = 0 := by simp
  refine ⟨kernel.lift h a ha, kernel.lift f (kernel.ι h ≫ kernel.ι g ≫ biprod.fst) hb, ?_, ?_⟩
  · apply (cancel_mono (kernel.ι f)).mp
    simp [a, Category.assoc]
  · apply (cancel_mono (kernel.ι h)).mp
    apply (cancel_mono (kernel.ι g)).mp
    simpa [a, Category.assoc] using hk.symm

/-- A module with a finite presentation is of finite presentation. -/
private theorem isFinitePresentation_of_presentation {C : Type u} [Category.{u} C]
    [HasBinaryProducts C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {S : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
    [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [∀ Y : C, HasSheafify (J.over Y) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    [∀ Y : C, (J.over Y).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
    {M : SheafOfModules.{u} S} (P : M.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] : M.IsFinitePresentation := by
  refine ⟨P.quasicoherentData.shrink, ⟨fun i => ⟨⟨?_⟩, ⟨?_⟩⟩⟩⟩
  · show Finite P.generators.I
    exact (show P.IsFinite from inferInstance).isFiniteType_generators.finite
  · show Finite P.relations.I
    exact (show P.IsFinite from inferInstance).isFiniteType_relations.finite

/-- The kernel of a map from a finite free module into a module with a global finite
presentation is of finite type. -/
private theorem kernel_free_to_globalPresentation_isFiniteType
    (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}) [IsCoherent (unit R)]
    (U : Opens X) (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (R.over U)) (P : N.Presentation) [P.IsFinite]
    (I : Type u) [Finite I] (f : free (R := R.over U) I ⟶ N) : (kernel f).IsFiniteType := by
  have hgen : Finite P.generators.I :=
    (show P.IsFinite from inferInstance).isFiniteType_generators.finite
  have : N.IsFinitePresentation := isFinitePresentation_of_presentation.{u} P
  set e : free (R := R.over U) I ⊞ free (R := R.over U) P.generators.I ≅
      free (R := R.over U) (I ⊕ P.generators.I) :=
    biprod.isoCoprod _ _ ≪≫ freeSumIso I P.generators.I with he
  set d : free (R := R.over U) I ⊞ free (R := R.over U) P.generators.I ⟶ N :=
    biprod.desc f P.generators.π with hd
  have : Epi d := biprod.epi_desc_of_epi_right f P.generators.π
  have : Epi (e.inv ≫ d) := by rw [hd]; infer_instance
  have hker : (kernel (e.inv ≫ d)).IsFiniteType :=
    LocalKernel.kernel_isFiniteType_of_epi_from_finite_free (e.inv ≫ d)
  have hd' : (kernel d).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (kernel.mapIso (e.inv ≫ d) d e.symm (Iso.refl _) (by simp))
  have : (kernel (kernel.ι d ≫ (biprod.snd :
      free (R := R.over U) I ⊞ free (R := R.over U) P.generators.I ⟶
        free (R := R.over U) P.generators.I))).IsFiniteType :=
    kernel_to_finite_free_isFiniteType R U P.generators.I _
  exact isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (kernelOfBiprodDescIso f P.generators.π).symm

/-- The same on the iterated slice site. -/
private theorem kernel_free_to_globalPresentation_over
    (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}) [IsCoherent (unit R)]
    (U : Opens X) (V : Over U) (N : SheafOfModules.{u} ((R.over U).over V))
    (P : N.Presentation) [P.IsFinite] (I : Type u) [Finite I]
    (f : free (R := (R.over U).over V) I ⟶ N) : (kernel f).IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  set E := overOverEquivalence (R := R) U V with hE
  have hpc : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{u, u} E.inverse := inferInstance
  set P' := P.map E.inverse (Iso.refl _) with hP'
  have : P'.IsFinite := by
    refine ⟨⟨?_⟩, ⟨?_⟩⟩
    · show Finite P.generators.I
      exact (show P.IsFinite from inferInstance).isFiniteType_generators.finite
    · show Finite P.relations.I
      exact (show P.IsFinite from inferInstance).isFiniteType_relations.finite
  set a := mapFreeIso E.inverse I (Iso.refl _) with ha
  have hg : (kernel (a.hom ≫ E.inverse.map f)).IsFiniteType :=
    kernel_free_to_globalPresentation_isFiniteType R V.left (E.inverse.obj N) P' I _
  have h₁ : (kernel (E.inverse.map f)).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_of_iso.{u}
      (kernel.mapIso (a.hom ≫ E.inverse.map f) (E.inverse.map f) a (Iso.refl _) (by simp))
  have h₂ : (E.inverse.obj (kernel f)).IsFiniteType :=
    isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (PreservesKernel.iso E.inverse f).symm
  exact isFiniteType_of_overOverEquivalence_inverse U V h₂

/-- The kernel of a map from a finite free module into a module of finite presentation, on a
slice site, is of finite type. -/
private theorem kernel_free_to_finitePresentation_isFiniteType
    (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}) [IsCoherent (unit R)]
    (U : Opens X) (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (R.over U)) [N.IsFinitePresentation]
    (I : Type u) [Finite I] (f : free (R := R.over U) I ⟶ N) : (kernel f).IsFiniteType := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation.exists_quasicoherentData N
  have hLocal : ∀ i, ((kernel f).over (q.X i)).IsFiniteType := by
    intro i
    have : (q.presentation i).IsFinite := hq.isFinite_presentation i
    have hg : (kernel ((freeOverIso (R.over U) (q.X i) I).hom ≫ f.over (q.X i))).IsFiniteType :=
      kernel_free_to_globalPresentation_over R U (q.X i) (N.over (q.X i))
        (q.presentation i) I _
    have h₁ : (kernel (f.over (q.X i))).IsFiniteType :=
      isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (kernel.mapIso
        ((freeOverIso (R.over U) (q.X i) I).hom ≫ f.over (q.X i)) (f.over (q.X i))
        (freeOverIso (R.over U) (q.X i) I) (Iso.refl _) (by simp))
    have : PreservesFiniteLimits (overFunctor.{u} (R.over U) (q.X i)) :=
      LocalCokernel.overFunctor_preservesFiniteLimits (q.X i)
    exact isFiniteType_of_iso.{u} (overKernelIso f (q.X i)).symm
  exact isFiniteType_of_coversTop (kernel f) q.X q.coversTop

/-- **Stacks 01BZ.** Over a ringed space whose structure sheaf is coherent as a module over
itself, a sheaf of modules is coherent if and only if it is of finite presentation. -/
@[stacks 01BZ]
theorem isCoherent_iff_isFinitePresentation
    (R : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}) (M : SheafOfModules.{u} R)
    [IsCoherent (unit R)] : IsCoherent M ↔ M.IsFinitePresentation := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    have : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent M := ⟨h.isFiniteType, h.kernel_isFiniteType⟩
    exact _root_.isFinitePresentation_of_isCoherent M
  · intro h
    refine ⟨inferInstance, fun U I hI f => ?_⟩
    have : (M.over U).IsFinitePresentation := isFinitePresentation_over M inferInstance U
    exact kernel_free_to_finitePresentation_isFiniteType R U (M.over U) I f

end RingedSpace

end Stacks.SheafOfModules
